## What's blocked

The third Step 6 proof point — a live WebSocket handshake to
`/api/realtime/socket` returning HTTP 101 — cannot be obtained as
PLAN.md specified. `/socket` is gated by `requireClarionRole('agent')`
(added in Phase 2, commit `04b863e`, predates this run), which requires
a resolved Clarion role regardless of `AUTH_ENFORCE`. Resolving a role
requires a session that passed `verifyFoundrySession`, which only
accepts JWTs signed by AuthPak's real private key (remote JWKS, no local
override in the vendored `@foundry/auth` package). There is no AuthPak
key available locally, and CLAUDE.md §12 forbids minting our own
AuthPak-equivalent tokens — so there is no honest way to pass the gate
under local `wrangler dev`.

This is a plan/codebase mismatch, not a defect in the migration. I did
not revert Steps 1–5: they're independently correct and verified, and
reverting the hosting migration would not unblock the WebSocket proof
either way (the role gate would reject the same request under Pages too).

Full root-cause writeup, evidence, and options are in the archived
PROGRESS.md's Step 6 log entry and Blockers section:
docs/runs/2026-07-15-workers-migration/PROGRESS.md

Steps 6 (WebSocket proof) through 10 (capstone/close-out) were not
attempted — they all sit downstream of this decision.

